 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: the entry al-Khuwārizmī of p. 392 goes on here. A speck (1.1 by 0.8 points) under the 5 of «35», 2.1-2.9 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L9: the s of the first «bis» is printed broken in three pieces; read s.",
  "col_left L11: «al-Kindī» has a bar over the last i, «Ya‘qūb» the sign of ‘ayn and a bar over the u, «Isḥāq» the ḥ sort.",
  "col_left L12, col_right L6, L7, L24, L34: several figures 3 have the ball of their upper stroke printed apart from the figure («310» and «313» in L12; «333» in R6; «337» and «338» in R7; «23» in R24; «301» in R34); it is not a point.",
  "col_left L15, L16: «‘Umar» begins with the sign of ‘ayn and «Muḥ.» has the ḥ sort; the m of «‘Umar» in L15 is printed broken, like ı and n.",
  "col_left L17: «*tables*» is printed in italics.",
  "col_left L19, L22: «*al-fihrist*» is printed with the italic fi ligature and «figurae» with the upright one; «an-Nadīm» has a bar over the i.",
  "col_left L22: «*ṣūrat*» has the dot under the s and a bar over the u; «*al-arḍ*» has the dot under the d.",
  "col_left L24: «κλῆρος τῆς τύχης» is Greek, read at 4,800 dpi: the circumflex of «κλῆρος» and «τῆς» is cast joined to the top of the η, «τύχης» has the acute on the υ; the κ is printed in its cursive form (ϰ).",
  "col_left L27: «κοίλωμα» is Greek, read at 4,800 dpi: the acute over the ι leans against the top of the λ; the κ is printed in its cursive form (ϰ).",
  "col_left L29: a round speck (1.1 by 1.1 points) under the 1 of «156», 3.2-4.3 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L30, L39: «*kramajyā*» and «*kunyah*» are printed in italics.",
  "col_left L31: the m of «Kremer» is printed broken, like ı and n.",
  "col_left L33: the K of «K.» is printed broken, its upper arm apart from the stem.",
  "col_left L34, L36: «*Ktābā da-nsīrē*» and «*Ktābā d-ḥārānāyē*» are printed in italics with bars over the long vowels; the h of «*ḥārānāyē*» has its dot below.",
  "col_left L40: «Kushāǵim» is printed with ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm. The mark under the point after «n.» is the top of the acute of the capital Ǵ in the line below (L41); specks far to the right of «n.» are not transcribed.",
  "col_left L41: «Kūshiyār» has bars over the u and the a, «Labbān» a bar over the second a, «al-Ǵīlī» the capital Ǵ and bars over both i. A thin curved stroke (about 4 by 2 points, 0.3-0.4 point thick), joined to the foot of the ā of «Labbān» and running down to the right under the n, is a flaw of the print and is not transcribed; it is not a sign of the transcription.",
  "col_left L43: «al-Kutubī» has a bar over the last i. A small speck to the right of «7.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L43, L44: a blank line separates the names in K from those in L.",
  "col_right L2: «λαμπήνη» is Greek, read at 4,800 dpi, with the acute on the η, cast joined to the top of the letter.",
  "col_right L9: «Langlès» is printed with a grave accent over the e.",
  "col_right L15: «*20*, *29* *30*;» is printed without a comma between 29 and 30; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_right L17: the a of «quartum» is printed broken, the lower part of its bowl drawn below the baseline like a dot below; read a. The m of the word is printed broken, like ı and n.",
  "col_right L18: the comma after «4)» is printed short (1.3 by 1.9 points, its foot 0.6 point below the baseline), like a point; read at 6,000 dpi, it has the round head and the short tail of a comma.",
  "col_right L28, L36: «Lēwī» has bars over the e and the i, «Gersōm» a bar over the o.",
  "col_right L28: a speck (0.7 by 0.8 point) between «ben» and «Gersōm», 3.4 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L29, L30: the first e of «stellae» in L29 and its last e in L30 are printed broken, open like c; read e. A small speck between «Leporis» and «stellae», 3.4 points below the baseline of L30, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L39: the L of the second small-capital numeral is printed broken, its foot apart from the stem; read {sc:xlii}.",
  "col_right L41: «Ḥarrānensis» has the dotted Ḥ and a bar over the a.",
  "col_right L43: the o of «observatoriis» is printed broken, open at the left; read o."
 ],
